Fix multi-GPU scanout on GPUs without KMS modifiers (AMD Polaris / MacBookPro15,1 dGPU).

`verifyDestinationDMABUF` compared the buffer's *modifier* against
`DRM_FORMAT_INVALID` (0) instead of `DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID` (0x00ffffffffffffff).
Since `initDRMFormats()` always appends `(DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID, external = true)`
("EGL can always do implicit modifiers"), a destination buffer with an implicit
modifier matched that entry and was rejected as "external-only" -- the exact
opposite of the intent of hyprwm/aquamarine#143.

It only bites GPUs that cannot advertise KMS modifiers: amdgpu sets
supportsAddFb2Modifiers only on GFX9+, so a Polaris scanout swapchain is allocated
modifier-less (modifier INVALID) and every cross-GPU blit to it is refused.
Symptom: monitor detected with a valid EDID and a workspace assigned, but black,
with an endless "Backend requires blit, but blit failed" retry loop in hyprland.log.

Already fixed upstream on main (present in v0.16.0); this backports it to 0.15.1 so
the fix drops in for Hyprland 0.56.2 without a SOVERSION 14 -> 15 relink.

Upstream: https://github.com/hyprwm/aquamarine/issues/220

--- a/src/backend/drm/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/drm/Renderer.cpp
@@ -1120,7 +1120,7 @@ bool CDRMRenderer::verifyDestinationDMABUF(const SDMABUFAttrs& attrs) {
         if (fmt.modifier != attrs.modifier)
             continue;
 
-        if (fmt.modifier != DRM_FORMAT_INVALID && fmt.external) {
+        if (fmt.modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID && fmt.external) {
             backend->log(AQ_LOG_ERROR, "EGL (verifyDestinationDMABUF): FAIL, format is external-only");
             return false;
         }
